# README stays current

Whenever you change user-visible or operator-facing behaviour in this repo, **update `README.md` in the same change** (same PR/commit when committing).

## Always sync README when you touch

- Features (Zigbee, HomeKit, remotes, groups, thermostat, sniffer, portal tabs/APIs)
- Hardware pins, UART, flash/partition layout, power notes
- Ports, setup codes, SoftAP names, OTA URLs/tags, branch roles (`main`/`dev`)
- Build/flash/erase steps, `PROJECT_VER` / versioning, CI workflows
- Limits (device/group counts), pairing/Touchlink flows, known caveats

## How to update

- Prefer editing the existing section over adding a duplicate “changelog” dump
- Bump or mention `PROJECT_VER` when the release version in `CMakeLists.txt` changes
- Remove claims that are no longer true; never leave “not implemented yet” for shipped features
- Keep the tone concise and factual (tables + short procedures)

## Do not

- Ship firmware-facing changes with a stale README
- Document internal-only refactors that users never see (unless they change build/flash steps)
